window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-5990f418af97b440"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"security\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">安全</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需查看完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。将 <code>.md</code> 附加到页面 URL 后，可查看该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>查找并修复代码中的漏洞。</p> <p>使用 Codex 调查代码和依赖项中的安全风险，然后制定并测试修复方案。你可以从代码库、代码变更或已有工具提供的发现结果开始。</p> <p><a id=\"find-vulnerabilities\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">查找漏洞</h2> <p>从扫描一个代码库开始，也可以进行更深入的审查或扫描多个代码库。你还可以在 CI 中自动运行扫描，在代码变更时或按计划检查代码。审阅扫描发现结果和覆盖范围，再决定下一步调查什么。</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/find-vulnerabilities-in-your-code\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">运行首次安全扫描（本地尚未收录）</a>：使用 Codex Security 插件扫描本地代码库，审阅证据和覆盖范围……</li> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/deep-security-scan\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">运行深度安全扫描（本地尚未收录）</a>：使用 Codex Security 插件对代码库或指定范围进行更全面的审计……</li> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/scan-multiple-repositories\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">扫描多个代码库（本地尚未收录）</a>：使用 Codex Security CLI 扫描指定提交版本的代码库清单，并逐一审阅……</li> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/automate-security-scans-in-ci\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">在 CI 中自动运行安全扫描（本地尚未收录）</a>：将 Codex Security CLI 添加到 CI 流水线中……</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"review-changes-and-dependencies\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">审查变更和依赖项</h2> <p>检查拉取请求或本地差异中是否存在安全回归问题，或评估代码库受到软件包公告或供应链安全公告影响的情况。先收集证据，再决定需要采取什么行动。</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/scan-code-changes-for-security\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">扫描代码变更中的安全问题（本地尚未收录）</a>：使用 Codex Security 插件检查基于 Git 的变更集，并验证合理的……</li> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/dependency-incident-audits\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">审计依赖项安全事件（本地尚未收录）</a>：使用 Codex 根据公开的软件包或供应链安全公告制定只读审计计划，然后……</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"fix-and-verify-findings\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">修复并验证发现的问题</h2> <p>针对经过审阅的扫描发现进行小范围修补，或处理现有的问题清单。准备合并之前，审阅每项变更及其验证证据。</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/fix-a-finding-from-your-security-scan\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">修复安全扫描发现的问题（本地尚未收录）</a>：使用 Codex Security 插件，根据经过审阅的扫描结果进行有针对性的修补。</li> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/remediate-vulnerability-backlog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">处理漏洞积压清单（本地尚未收录）</a>：导入已批准的问题，例如来自工单工具或漏洞报告系统的发现，然后使用……</li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"security\">Security</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Find and fix vulnerabilities in your code.</p> <p>Use Codex to investigate security risks in your code and dependencies, then develop and test fixes. Start with a repository, a code change, or findings from tools you already use.</p> <h2 id=\"find-vulnerabilities\">Find vulnerabilities</h2> <p>Start with a scan of one repository, run a deeper review, or scan a repository inventory. Automate scans in CI to review code on a schedule or as it changes. Review the findings and coverage to decide where to investigate next.</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/find-vulnerabilities-in-your-code\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Run your first security scan (not in this local snapshot)</a>: Use the Codex Security plugin to scan a local repository, review the evidence and coverage...</li> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/deep-security-scan\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Run a deep security scan (not in this local snapshot)</a>: Use the Codex Security plugin to run a more comprehensive audit of a repository or scoped...</li> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/scan-multiple-repositories\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Scan multiple repositories (not in this local snapshot)</a>: Use the Codex Security CLI to scan a list of repositories at specific commits, review each...</li> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/automate-security-scans-in-ci\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Automate security scans in CI (not in this local snapshot)</a>: Add the Codex Security CLI to your CI pipeline</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"review-changes-and-dependencies\">Review changes and dependencies</h2> <p>Check a pull request or local diff for security regressions, or assess your repository's exposure to a package or supply chain advisory. Gather evidence before deciding what needs action.</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/scan-code-changes-for-security\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Scan code changes for security (not in this local snapshot)</a>: Use the Codex Security plugin to examine a Git-backed change set, validate plausible...</li> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/dependency-incident-audits\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Audit dependency incidents (not in this local snapshot)</a>: Use Codex to turn a public package or supply chain advisory into a read-only audit, then...</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"fix-and-verify-findings\">Fix and verify findings</h2> <p>Turn a reviewed scan finding into a focused patch, or work through findings from an existing backlog. Review each change and its verification evidence before preparing it for merge.</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/fix-a-finding-from-your-security-scan\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Fix a finding from your security scan (not in this local snapshot)</a>: Use the Codex Security plugin to turn a reviewed scan finding into a focused patch</li> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/remediate-vulnerability-backlog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Remediate a vulnerability backlog (not in this local snapshot)</a>: Bring in approved findings from ticketing tools or vulnerability reporting systems, then use...</li> </ul>"};
